# Registers HtmlSanitizerExtensions, so the Java binding's types pick up Groovy
# operators (<<, +, -, in, [], .text) without being wrapped. Wrapping would be
# the wrong move: Node and Attribute are borrowed views that die when sanitize
# returns, and a wrapper is exactly the thing someone retains by accident.
moduleName=htmlsanitizer-groovy
moduleVersion=1.0.0
extensionClasses=org.htmlsanitizer.groovy.HtmlSanitizerExtensions
